From: kevinzhow <kevinzhow@local>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 21:00:53 +0800
Subject: libx264 registers as libx264_sw

The name libx264 goes to this project's H.264 encoder (hardware through the Android codec bridge,
software otherwise), so applications that ask for libx264 by name get it; the x264 encoder stays
available as libx264_sw, which that encoder uses as its software fallback.

Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-09-26
X-Rungic-Status: Inappropriate [makes room for the Android hardware codec under the name applications ask for]
X-Rungic-Tests: L3:codec.hw
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/54 docs/research/35
---
 libavcodec/libx264.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavcodec/libx264.c b/libavcodec/libx264.c
index b688d4f..6adb666 100644
--- a/libavcodec/libx264.c
+++ b/libavcodec/libx264.c
@@ -1608,7 +1608,7 @@ static const AVClass x264_class = {
 };
 
 const FFCodec ff_libx264_encoder = {
-    .p.name           = "libx264",
+    .p.name           = "libx264_sw",
     CODEC_LONG_NAME("libx264 H.264 / AVC / MPEG-4 AVC / MPEG-4 part 10"),
     .p.type           = AVMEDIA_TYPE_VIDEO,
     .p.id             = AV_CODEC_ID_H264,
